        {
          "source_quote": "ἄλλως δὲ οὐδ’ ἂν τέκνον ἢ ἀδελφὸς ἢ φίλος ἢ ἄλλως πως ποτὲ γένους μοι ἀνήκων, ἐάνπερ ἀνάξιος ᾖ, τοῦδε μὴ μεταδοῦναι χάριν, ὡς οὐ προσῆκεν.",
          "english_quote": "Otherwise—not even a child or a brother or a friend or anyone ever related to me in any other way, if indeed he is unworthy—not to pass on any of this as a favor, since it is not proper.",
          "issue": "The English preserves a fragment but does not establish a secure correspondence between its grammatical relationships and those of the supplied Greek. The construction with οὐδ’ ἂν and the nominative persons lacks an expressed governing predicate; the relationship of τοῦδε, μεταδοῦναι, and χάριν remains unresolved. In particular, 'any of this as a favor' combines two provisional interpretations that cannot presently be certified. Consequently, complete propositional coverage, absence of added meaning, and the scope of the opening negation cannot be affirmed. The draft correctly discloses this problem, but disclosure does not make the rendering acceptable. The supplied print verification establishes the wording, not its interpretation; this is not demonstrated OCR error or textual corruption.",
          "suggested_revision": "Keep publication blocked pending a defensible grammatical and lexical analysis of the supplied sentence, particularly οὐδ’ ἂν and τοῦδε μὴ μεταδοῦναι χάριν. Preserve the unresolved alternatives explicitly rather than inventing a finite predicate or silently changing word division. If an emendation is proposed, distinguish its exact Greek wording from the supplied reading and provide supporting evidence. No replacement English is accepted at this stage.",
          "severity": "blocking"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "τὸν θάνατον ὑποπτεύσαι",
          "english_quote": "anticipate death",
          "issue": "ὑποπτεύσαι expresses suspicion or apprehension. 'Anticipate death' can suggest a firmer expectation and does not clearly preserve that speculative force.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider 'suspect that I may die' within the conditional sentence. This proposed wording requires fresh review in context.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἄξιος εἶναι τῆς πίστεως",
          "english_quote": "worthy of the faith",
          "issue": "The immediate context concerns property entrusted to a bishop and its eventual return to a qualified child. The construction ἄξιος τῆς πίστεως therefore strongly supports worthiness of trust, rather than worthiness of the religious faith. The note acknowledges 'trust' but privileges 'faith' primarily because the setting is ecclesial; that does not adequately address the fiduciary context or the construction itself. The earlier reference to the bishop holding the same faith need not determine this occurrence's sense.",
          "suggested_revision": "Compare the proposed main-text rendering 'worthy of trust' with 'worthy of the faith'. Document the contextual reason for distinguishing this occurrence from τὴν αὐτὴν ἔχοντι πίστιν, and retain the religious-faith interpretation as an alternative if it remains viable. Any revised clause must undergo fresh review.",
